{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I’d assess **economic viability, not AUM alone**:\n\n- **Break-even:** Compare fee revenue and other sponsor income with operating, legal, licensing, marketing, and distribution costs. Low-fee or costly strategies may need more scale.\n- **Who covers shortfalls:** Review waivers, expense caps, subsidy commitments, end dates, and the sponsor’s capacity to absorb losses.\n- **Seed durability:** Determine whether assets are affiliated or independent, concentrated or locked up, and likely to persist. Temporary seed can exaggerate demand.\n- **Flows and liquidity:** Monitor net flows, holder concentration, spreads, trading volume, and market-maker support. Outflows or fragile liquidity can increase costs.\n- **Sponsor behavior:** Consider financial resources, launch record, stated scale thresholds, and history of consolidating or closing funds.\n\nThese are warning signs, not a closure forecast."}}
